WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Two French phrases, just
a couple of letters apart:

2
00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.280
«en effet» and «en fait».

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:10.330
Swap them, and your argument says
the opposite of what you meant.

4
00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.310
One model paragraph runs: concede,

5
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:17.680
confirm, contrast, key fact, conclusion.

6
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.730
Take away its five small words,

7
00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.090
and what's left?

8
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.130
Why can those small words
between your ideas matter

9
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.540
more than the ideas themselves?

10
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.610
In this mission, you'll
build an argument skeleton,

11
00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.070
with each connector doing one job.

12
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.040
Then you'll drag connectors into
a paragraph about electric cars,

13
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.830
one slot at a time.

14
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: find out what
the small words really do.
